  "body": "Split off from #820 (mod vises, PR stacked on #823).\n\n**What:** two follow-ups to the mod-vise pair (`PlaceModVisePair`, `modvise::JawParams`):\n\n1. **Dual-station block.** A wider block that carries two jaw faces (two stations side by side, or a centre block clamping toward both sides), placed on the grid the same way and fitted per station. The single fixed/adjustable pair landed in #820; a dual-station variant needs either a second clamping face in `JawParams` or a third block kind, and a fit that takes two stocks (or one stock per station).\n2. **Edit and re-fit a placed pair.** Today a pair is placed once, fitted to the stock as it stands. Changing a block's figures (`SetModJaw`, regenerating its mesh through `UpdateModel` as `SetVise` does) and re-fitting the adjustable block after the stock changes (re-pick its hole and slide, one undo step) are not there yet; a pair is re-placed by undo and place again.\n\nBoth: MCP tools (`set_mod_jaw`, a dual-station preset/flag on `add_mod_vise_pair`), the plate row's UI, save/load through the `mod_jaw` key (move it onto #830's `fixture_keys` reader if that has landed).\n\n**Done means:** a dual-station block can be placed on the grid and fitted, and a placed pair can be edited and re-fitted in one undo step each, pinned by tests like `crates/app/tests/mod_vise.rs`.\n\nPart of #339. Follow-up of #820.\n",
